{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence","id":1517804,"title":"Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani's success makes me question the Council of Nines competence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-12T12:13:48-07:00","id":1517804,"title":"Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani's success makes me question the Council of Nines competence","content":"Now it\u2019s well known that the Ahl-I-Batin left the Council of Nine due to the general lack of concern the Council of Nine had towards the Middle East. Long story short, they ended up using the Taftani as Union bait, and with their aid, they were able to push the Union out of the Middle East. But it doesn't just stop there, the Ahl-I-Batin decided to cement their status as protectors of the Middle East by getting involved in its politics and have been shown to increase their web of influence. The Taftani however seem to be going in a different direction, while most Taftani are more interested in staying in their little territories, a growing number seem to have decided to spread their influence outside of the Middle East.<br /> <br /> Afridi, <b>The</b> drug lord of Afghanistan, who sells opium and hashish to the Russians and Cartels, who would then distribute it in Technocracy entrenched countries, believes by getting the citizens of those countries addicted and weakened, he can undermine the Technocracy. He's not above-using mind magick to do it either. This has both made him rich and #1 on the Technocratic kill list, although it doesn't seem like they will be able to get rid of him anytime soon, as they have already sent three assault teams with all of them disappearing. He also had 3 out of 4 Russian soldiers who were occupying Afghanistan addicted to smoking opium or mainlining heroin, it was stated that this addiction stayed with them even when they went back to Russia. He also takes credit for their defeat as he would cut off the supply of any soldier he felt fought too enthusiastically, sending them into withdrawal.<br /> <br /> Bin-Jadis used the wealth he gained from the Oil Crisis, to create a sanctum in the Arabic district of Harlem in New York. He proceeded to buy a theater to turn into a second sanctum and has become a major political player in New York, with a liberal use of mind magick of course. He has made it to where the Arabic district is now recognized as \u201cLittle Arabia\u201d, and is now reminiscent of what you would see in the Middle East. Even the street signs are in Arabic. He was also the catalyst behind Disney releasing Aladdin and has already talked the local school board into teaching Arabian Nights. This all goes towards affecting the Technocratic Paradigm on a larger scale.<br /> <br /> Now you must be wondering, how can I claim that a growing number of Taftani are spreading their influence when I only mentioned two? Well, there's not just those two but also their apprentices. It was explicitly stated that Afridi does not hold the same tendency as most Taftani for isolationism, as he has a small army of gunmen, <b>apprentices</b>, consorts, and djinn, and no doubt Bin-Jadis will take on some of his own. No doubt their apprentices will follow the same path as their masters and will likely decide to keep in contact with their peers to further each other's political power and weaken the technocratic paradigm.<br /> <br /> All this is to say, is that from the way I see it, the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani have accomplished more in 60-70 years, than the 5-6 centuries the Council of Nine have existed for.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T13:07:08-07:00","id":1517810,"title":"","content":"Maybe you could retcon the Technocracy as focusing so much on the Traditions that they ignored these guys to their own detriment. <br /> <br /> just spitballing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T13:56:03-07:00","id":1517817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1517810#post1517810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you could retcon the Technocracy as focusing so much on the Traditions that they ignored these guys to their own detriment.<br /> <br /> just spitballing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that would work, feels kinda weird ignoring a druglord and a craft of dramatic suicide bombers tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-12-2023, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T14:49:26-07:00","id":1517827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1517817#post1517817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that would work, feels kinda weird ignoring a druglord and a craft of dramatic suicide bombers tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are area limited and take themselves out of the picture. The Two you described are subtle influences that use the tools of the Technocracy to bring about their ideas. It's not the Taftani as a whole who are a threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T15:35:31-07:00","id":1517834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1517827#post1517827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are area limited and take themselves out of the picture. The Two you described are subtle influences that use the tools of the Technocracy to bring about their ideas. It's not the Taftani as a whole who are a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, Taftani tend to have close student-mentor relationships, I believe it is also the norm for Taftani to have multiple apprentices. It is likely that those two will pass on the lessons and skills that they have learned to their apprentices, and when their aprentices gain students of their own, they will pass on those teachings to them.<br /> <br /> Edit:Also M20 mentioned Taftani getting subtler","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-13-2023, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T03:54:47-07:00","id":1517931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1517834#post1517834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I remember correctly, Taftani tend to have close student-mentor relationships, I believe it is also the norm for Taftani to have multiple apprentices. It is likely that those two will pass on the lessons and skills that they have learned to their apprentices, and when their aprentices gain students of their own, they will pass on those teachings to them.<br /> <br /> Edit:Also M20 mentioned Taftani getting subtler</div> </div> </div> </div>So. Lost Paths is a brilliant book. the portrayal of both the factions is quite through and interesting. However, you seem to be under a very odd impression that either of these two factions are large enough to be relevant. There is around 50 000 mages in the world, going by Fallen Tower. Of those, the vast majority will be Traditions and Technocracy. Let's say that there is about 10% of this number allotted to the Crafts (and that's generous). This means that across all the Crafts there is maybe 5000 Magi. Taftani are well known to be one of the smaller crafts, so putting their number to say 50 is probably incredibly generous. That's the total - in their Umbral palaces, in their secret caves, in their magical valleys and in the places where they even managed to sabotage the Technocratic paradigm. They are neither numerous, they are not broadly spread nor are they particularly dangerous (especially as most of the time they're happy in their places of power fighting each other), especially compared to what the Technocracy has to deal with on a day to day basis.<br /> <br /> Now you might consider their two sample characters as highly efficient Ascension Warriors, and that's a correct assessment of those two guys. However, keep in mind that they are the biggest legends of the Taftani, these are their Dantes, Porthoses and Voormases. So if you're going to say that they are &quot;more&quot; competent consider who they should be compared to.<br /> <br /> As for the apprentice thing. That's just silly. The whole apprenticeship of the Taftani is an incredibly complex and intimate affair, one that's hard on the master and the apprentice. They don't have more than one apprentice at the time and I can imagine that most Taftani will never really even want to have more than one in their lifetime, after all, the stark individualism and pride of the Craft make them their own greatest enemies and provoke them to fight over the stupidest matters of philosophy.<br /> <br /> So, no. Taftani are not especially better at Ascension War. Arguably, looking how hidebound and self destroying they tend to be, they're probably worse than the average Ascension Warrior. They have some brilliant Ascension Warriors, but there are many such luminaries in the world with a bigger impact than them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T04:07:29-07:00","id":1517932,"title":"","content":"You should also be mindful of what differant groups hope to achieve. The tafitani ultimatly want to carve out a niche territory and pursue their personal aghehda wereas the 9mts are fighting a 3 way war for the soul of the sleepers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T11:41:16-07:00","id":1517964,"title":"","content":"And I understand that, but for an organization that has been around for 5 centuries with traditions that originate from continents as far as Asia, each of which was around for centuries before they joined the council, you would think they would at least have gained control over a few countries, which would have made it a lot easier in fighting for sleeper souls. Politically, they should at least be dominating a few Asian and African countries. Australia has also been shown to have little Technocratic presence at the moment, and the Traditions should be focusing manpower on dominating it before the Technocracy takes over another potential superpower.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Taftani, true they want to carve out a territory for themselves and pursue personal agendas, but at the same time they want to spread Asha ( the truth) and destroy the Druj (the lie), and in the pursuit of doing that, they have begun to harm the technocracy far more than the traditions ever did. Because of the Taftani and their flair for flouting consensus and paradox, as well as their tendency to go out with a bang, there are zones within the middle east where the technocratic paradigm simply doesn't function. And by M20 they have evolved to where they are now using the tools of the technocracy against them.\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T17:02:02-07:00","id":1517993,"title":"","content":"Again. By what standard and whose definition? Who cares for territory and control of nations when you can control the fate of humanity and the laws of reality? Does Technocracy control &quot;a few countries&quot; ? Have you read the history of the Traditions? Do you know how many contributions to human culture and history stem from their efforts? They were never fighting for the control of territory, they were fighting for the control of people's imaginations.<br /> <br /> By that lens, Taftani are small time warlords in a small and forgotten piece of land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T18:17:36-07:00","id":1517994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1517993#post1517993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again. By what standard and whose definition? Who cares for territory and control of nations when you can control the fate of humanity and the laws of reality? Does Technocracy control &quot;a few countries&quot; ? Have you read the history of the Traditions? Do you know how many contributions to human culture and history stem from their efforts? They were never fighting for the control of territory, they were fighting for the control of people's imaginations.<br /> <br /> By that lens, Taftani are small time warlords in a small and forgotten piece of land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Controlling a country would help in controlling the fates of at least a portion of humanity and the laws of reality within that country. It would definitely make it easier to spread propaganda and affect the beliefs of its citizens, in turn affecting reality, similar to how technocracy spreads its paradigm. It would also help fund efforts in controlling the fates of the rest of humanity as well as affecting the laws of reality in other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy also definitely does control countries, though in a subtle way, through both politics and media, with the syndicate having an entire methodology for media control, in which their effects division put subliminal messaging in everything from tv shows to video games to subtly push sleepers into the technocratic paradigm. They also control entire corporations, have agents in all major crime organizations, have agents acting as all types of law enforcement such as police, judges, and lawyers, and also have prison managers. The NWO itself has been said to have both government agents and intelligence operatives as personnel, many of whom hold positions of some importance, they also hold power in academia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T06:26:58-07:00","id":1518028,"title":"","content":"Which edition's Technocracy? And do you actually believe that world would be in such a mess if the Technocracy actually controlled it? Technocracy is powerful and the dominant group of Mages on the planet. But try as they might, they do not control the world.<br /> <br /> As for the Traditions, do you think they lack money, influence or cultural resonance considering that most of them are built on cultural cornerstones? The point is that most of them just want to be left alone and do their thing. Those of them that want to change the world can and have done so, as the Tradition books and the upcoming Lore of Traditions are more then happy to point out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T07:57:42-07:00","id":1518033,"title":"","content":"Yeah part of the reason why the modern Crafts exist is that they've basically fallen through the cracks between the Technocracy and the Traditions with part of that being that they keep their heads downs from the Ascension War and stick to their own little corners of the world. As a result, the Traditions don't care about them and they're far down the list of threats that the Technocracy ignores them for the most part.<br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with how successful or not they've been. In fact it can be argued that because they are so limited in their influence and reach in the world that they aren't actually successful, merely small groups hiding away from the Big Boys they could never hope to challenge seriously and just trying to survive in the shadows of giants.<br /> <br /> Well until the Crafts began banding together and the Disparate Alliance was born. Which honestly is pretty much the biggest success any of the Crafts have had in a long time. Even if we never get anything further on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T08:24:38-07:00","id":1518035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518028#post1518028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which edition's Technocracy? And do you actually believe that world would be in such a mess if the Technocracy actually controlled it? Technocracy is powerful and the dominant group of Mages on the planet. But try as they might, they do not control the world.<br /> <br /> As for the Traditions, do you think they lack money, influence or cultural resonance considering that most of them are built on cultural cornerstones? The point is that most of them just want to be left alone and do their thing. Those of them that want to change the world can and have done so, as the Tradition books and the upcoming Lore of Traditions are more then happy to point out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying they control the world, just that they control countries like America, England, and Japan. And even then, they can't control every aspect of life, messes are bound to happen. Regarding the Traditions, I admit that they have affected the world and were the catalysts for many of its changes. They do have resources as well, but compared to the Technocracy, it's very little. Technocracy has far more money and influence than the Traditions will ever have, mainly because they have entire conventions that are responsible for bringing in money and building influence. Each convention has a job that they stick to. The traditions on the other hand are more focused on the abstract such as enlightenment/ascension, they don't have one Tradition whose responsible for managing fianance and building weaponry, a majority of the traditions also lack the cohesion that conventions tend to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T09:11:25-07:00","id":1518039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518033#post1518033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah part of the reason why the modern Crafts exist is that they've basically fallen through the cracks between the Technocracy and the Traditions with part of that being that they keep their heads downs from the Ascension War and stick to their own little corners of the world. As a result, the Traditions don't care about them and they're far down the list of threats that the Technocracy ignores them for the most part.<br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with how successful or not they've been. In fact it can be argued that because they are so limited in their influence and reach in the world that they aren't actually successful, merely small groups hiding away from the Big Boys they could never hope to challenge seriously and just trying to survive in the shadows of giants.<br /> <br /> Well until the Crafts began banding together and the Disparate Alliance was born. Which honestly is pretty much the biggest success any of the Crafts have had in a long time. Even if we never get anything further on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Lost Paths, the Technocracy was exterminating crafts and was trying to exterminate both the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani. They were focused on taking control of the middle east. They were only pushed out by the concentrated efforts of the Batin and Taftani. Yes, the Traditions were their number one enemies, but that doesn't mean that they will ignore that crafts exist, and even though they were of little threat, they still chose to pursue extermination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:10:08-07:00","id":1518096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518039#post1518039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Lost Paths, the Technocracy was exterminating crafts and was trying to exterminate both the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani. They were focused on taking control of the middle east. They were only pushed out by the concentrated efforts of the Batin and Taftani. Yes, the Traditions were their number one enemies, but that doesn't mean that they will ignore that crafts exist, and even though they were of little threat, they still chose to pursue extermination.</div> </div> </div> </div>... what? That's not what that book says.This whole thread has prompted me to take it down and go over it the last few days and enjoy the excellent stuff within. The two factions have nothing to do with each other and don't spend any page count on each other. The Batini are (as ever) the subtle ones influencing certain people and certain places and seeking to keep the Web of Faith and Mount Qaf operational. The Taftani? They kicked out the Technocracy in '78 with kicking out the Syndicate and their &quot;project&quot;. Technocracy stopped bothering them by 1991.<br /> <br /> The book was published in May 2001 and written months before that. None of what followed in the Middle East was accounted for, or how the world would change drastically after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:45:32-07:00","id":1518103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518096#post1518096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... what? That's not what that book says.This whole thread has prompted me to take it down and go over it the last few days and enjoy the excellent stuff within. The two factions have nothing to do with each other and don't spend any page count on each other. The Batini are (as ever) the subtle ones influencing certain people and certain places and seeking to keep the Web of Faith and Mount Qaf operational. The Taftani? They kicked out the Technocracy in '78 with kicking out the Syndicate and their &quot;project&quot;. Technocracy stopped bothering them by 1991.<br /> <br /> The book was published in May 2001 and written months before that. None of what followed in the Middle East was accounted for, or how the world would change drastically after that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly the union were in conflict with both taftani and batin, and to survive the batin had to turn union attention towards the Taftani. And in the Afridi section it was mentionned how while the union were going after crafts Afridis name kept popping up which prompted them to go after him.<br /> <br /> I might need to look through that agian, but I was pretty sure that was the gist of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T19:01:22-07:00","id":1518119,"title":"","content":"Let's remember which parts of the planet the Mage factions influence. The Batini and the Taftani are major influences in limited areas of the planet. The two crafts share influence in areas that are basically poor (the oil wealth is sometimes called the &quot;resource curse&quot;), war torn, mainly infertile, and culturally stagnant. The Technocracy and the Traditions struggle over the richest, most populous, dynamic, and influential, sections of the planet.<br /> <br /> If either the Technocracy or the Traditions hold these areas for another century, it won't be hard to slowly but steadily force paradigmic conformity on the rest. Prosperity and stability will require it. If Afghanistan is still violent, backwards, impoverished, and ruled by drug lords a hundred years from now, it won't really change the world at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T19:37:55-07:00","id":1518123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518119#post1518119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's remember which parts of the planet the Mage factions influence. The Batini and the Taftani are major influences in limited areas of the planet. The two crafts share influence in areas that are basically poor (the oil wealth is sometimes called the &quot;resource curse&quot;), war torn, mainly infertile, and culturally stagnant. The Technocracy and the Traditions struggle over the richest, most populous, dynamic, and influential, sections of the planet.<br /> <br /> If either the Technocracy or the Traditions hold these areas for another century, it won't be hard to slowly but steadily force paradigmic conformity on the rest. Prosperity and stability will require it. If Afghanistan is still violent, backwards, impoverished, and ruled by drug lords a hundred years from now, it won't really change the world at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there's mention in M20 of Taftani holding power within Dubai, there was also Jadis who is still a major political player in New York, and Afridi who has a stranglehold over the drug operation in Afghanistan and was quite similar to Pablo Escabor in some respects. It would also be logical to assume that the Batin have subtle control over Saudi Arabia and at least some power over the royal family.<br /> <br /> But details like that seem to have been left out/ignored/dropped entirely. The metaplot is probably going to go back to focusing on Trads vs Techs. If they do include the Disparates, they are probably just going to act as the Trads 2.0.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T06:54:55-07:00","id":1518239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518123#post1518123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there's mention in M20 of Taftani holding power within Dubai</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth to mention that they accomplished this by adopting a much more subtle approach to their magick, which can be regarded as a concession to the Technocratic Paradigm.<br /> <br /> In general, Crafts hold great power over small areas. They can overpower the factions in some very specific places, but don't have the kind of world-spanning influence that the factions have. They can defeat the Technocracy/Traditions because they aren't focusing their resources on them, but rather on a more &quot;global domination&quot; level<br /> <br /> Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani ARE notable in the sense that the former have done very large feats of diplomacy and magick, and the latter are very hard to figth on their own turf.<br /> <br /> These are no small feats, but I don't think that it's enough to declare them a bigger threat. After all, as has been mentioned in the thread, the majority of the metaplot events and big names aren't related to the Crafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-18-2023, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T08:44:08-07:00","id":1518246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518239#post1518239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth to mention that they accomplished this by adopting a much more subtle approach to their magick, which can be regarded as a concession to the Technocratic Paradigm.<br /> <br /> In general, Crafts hold great power over small areas. They can overpower the factions in some very specific places, but don't have the kind of world-spanning influence that the factions have. They can defeat the Technocracy/Traditions because they aren't focusing their resources on them, but rather on a more &quot;global domination&quot; level<br /> <br /> Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani ARE notable in the sense that the former have done very large feats of diplomacy and magick, and the latter are very hard to figth on their own turf.<br /> <br /> These are no small feats, but I don't think that it's enough to declare them a bigger threat. After all, as has been mentioned in the thread, the majority of the metaplot events and big names aren't related to the Crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, I'm not saying that they can go toe to toe with them, I just believe having multiple countries in close proximity under a faction's control would make it easier for them to expand into other territories. This would make them a potentially larger threat, maybe not now, but definitely in the future if their growth goes unchecked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T10:32:30-07:00","id":1518257,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, a huge part of the history of Mage involved the Traditions and Technocracy picking up the idiot ball whenever it is convenient. Indeed both factions are basically long periods of ineffectiveness or laziness punctuated by short bursts of supreme competence.<br /> <br /> Possibly the better interpretation is a long and convoluted shadow war full of named offensives and gambits, with world shaking (or ending) consequences narrowly avoided several times a century. That is, we can presume both factions have been very effective and it only seems otherwise because we don\u2019t see just how much energy they put into countering each other or what the world would be like if they ran unopposed.<br /> <br /> Outside of a few key events, though, we don\u2019t usually see that so it is easier to consider the former than the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T11:17:13-07:00","id":1518259,"title":"","content":"None knows what the future holds.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't say they have multiple countries &quot;under their control&quot;, yet. They have influence there, but the territory where they've kicked out the Technocracy it's much smaller: Taftani have the city of Dubai, also the city of Petra I think, and the Empty Quarter (larger than a small country, but also emptier and not very influential). <br /> <br /> Batini &quot;territory&quot; it's much larger, but they also have a much more tenuous hold over it. Remember that the Batini wouldn't need to rebuild the Web of Faith if the Technocracy hadn't kicked their asses there in the first place. To say the territory within the Web of Faith it's &quot;under Batini control&quot; may be too generous. Both the Traditions and the Technocracy have power over there. It's far from uncontested<br /> <br /> Them both joining together in the Alliance it's their best bet to win more influence against the Technocracy and the Traditions, but one has to see if the whole thing last. Remember that they're ancient enemies, joined together against a common foe. The moment they feel secure things may go south","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T15:25:15-07:00","id":1518328,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say that Dubai is Taftani anymore as <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> revealed that there is a Syn-ItX Construct there that is actively contesting the Craft's presence there and effectively turning the city into a battleground of influence between the two groups. So it's not really Taftani Stronghold anymore. In fact the only part of the Middle East that we know the Technocracy hasn't gained much ground is Iran where the Ahl-I-Batin's grip has proven difficult to crack. Though may not be the most flattering thing for Ahl-I-Batin given some of the stuff that's gone on in Iran in recent years.<br /> <br /> And for those that haven't read or don't have said book, the general attitude towards the Middle East for the Union is that they are only really being held back by the Crafts and the need for resources in other regions as the Masses are accepting the Technocratic Paradigm just fine. So yeah the efforts of the Taftani and Ahl-I-Batin haven't really been all that successful in keeping the Technocracy out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T18:43:50-07:00","id":1518340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518328#post1518328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say that Dubai is Taftani anymore as <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> revealed that there is a Syn-ItX Construct there that is actively contesting the Craft's presence there and effectively turning the city into a battleground of influence between the two groups. So it's not really Taftani Stronghold anymore. In fact the only part of the Middle East that we know the Technocracy hasn't gained much ground is Iran where the Ahl-I-Batin's grip has proven difficult to crack. Though may not be the most flattering thing for Ahl-I-Batin given some of the stuff that's gone on in Iran in recent years.<br /> <br /> And for those that haven't read or don't have said book, the general attitude towards the Middle East for the Union is that they are only really being held back by the Crafts and the need for resources in other regions as the Masses are accepting the Technocratic Paradigm just fine. So yeah the efforts of the Taftani and Ahl-I-Batin haven't really been all that successful in keeping the Technocracy out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, guess this whole thing was pointless. At this point, might as well rename the game T:ATB, Technocracy: And Their Bitches. Foreshadowing for a new post perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T21:08:05-07:00","id":1518345,"title":"","content":"It's more complicated than that. And I had a whole lengthy post about that but I seem to be cursed and keep losing it because I can post it.<br /> <br /> So I will keep this short because I am tried of writing it out again and again only to lose it.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy has been the dominant force in MtAs, they haven't actually gotten closer to achieving their goals in over at least a hundred years. Not because of the Mages or other Supernaturals but because of the Masses. Yes, the Masses have embraced Technology but that's really all they have. Science-denying Flat-Earthers and Anti-vaxxers not only still exist but are thriving. Hate-mongering nationalists and religious fundamentalists endure and rally against the unified, scientific world they wish to create.<br /> <br /> In the end, the Union is now stuck dealing with the various Supernatural threats and mundane problems like climate change while also having to fight against the stupidity and willful ignorance of the Masses.<br /> <br /> Hell, the introduction of <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> starts with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We\u2019re losing.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know what you\u2019ve been told, kiddies: Our magnificent Union cornered the market on Consensus. Mankind\u2019s curled up with their smart phones, everyone loves technology, and cybernetic monkeys fly out my ass on command, raining fire on the poor little sorcerers cowering in the shadows of our magnificent Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I ask you this: Does it look like we are winning?<br /> <br /> Irrationality rules the day. Our world unravels at the seams. If our sad-sack species has formed any kind of consensus, it\u2019s that cutting off your nose to spite your face is much more fun when you use a chainsaw in public to do it.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re partly to blame for this, you know. We got stupid, careless, so caught up in our own propaganda that we refused to see the infection eating us alive.<br /> <br /> Worst of all, we got complacent. We believed it would only take a few surgical strikes on the worst offenders, and a wealth of luxuries for the Masses, before humanity would come around and enter a grand age of civil stability.<br /> <br /> We were wrong.<br /> <br /> Man is fundamentally irrational. He wants ghosts and vampires and boy wizards with English accents. He wants to believe that genital configurations or melanin production define him as blessed in the eyes of nonexistent gods. He doesn\u2019t fear Apocalypse \u2014 he craves it, so long as he doesn\u2019t have to live personally with the results. He\u2019s more fascinated with wanking off in the mirror than with looking toward the horizon of what he could be if he\u2019d just get his hand off his cock.<br /> <br /> Man cannot be trusted with the future. If we are to have a future, that future must belong to us.<br /> <br /> Kids, we dropped the ball. Our enemies have it in play, and they\u2019re sprinting toward the goalposts.<br /> <br /> If they score one more time, they win.<br /> <br /> Our enemies play for keeps.<br /> <br /> But, so do we.<br /> <br /> So, get back in the game, my friends, and remove your heads from your asses before we lose it all.\u200b </div> </div> </div>A far cry from the more triumphant introduction of it's predecessor, <i>Guide to the Technocracy</i>. And throughout the book we get other Technocrats just frustrated with the Masses over their willful apathy and ignorance. In one section, a veteran field operative describes humanity stupidity as the worst thing that any agent will encounter, as while the supernaturals can cause all manner of headaches, they haven't started world wars or endangered the planet with nuclear Armageddon.<br /> <br /> It's also a bit of a continuation of the collective apathy of the Masses from Rev Ed where no one really won the Ascension War and it ended up largely being a pointless waste because the Masses decided that they didn't care about all that Ascension business and would rather wallow in the mud of apathy and ignorance.<br /> <br /> I will also add that while the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani haven't really held out all that well against the Technocracy, the Disparate Alliance might actually be a real success for them and more importantly, are targeting a much more serious threat to the world, the Nephandi. Who have kind of become a blind spot for the Traditions and Technocracy. Yes, both do fight them but not nearly as much as they do each other. And depending on your Metaplot setup, may have become the unwitting dupes of the Nephandi. So one could argue that while the Traditions and Technocracy have become fixated on their conflict and a goal that is perhaps impossible, even for Mages, the Disparates are focusing their attention to a much real threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T21:37:25-07:00","id":1518346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518345#post1518345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more complicated than that. And I had a whole lengthy post about that but I seem to be cursed and keep losing it because I can post it.<br /> <br /> So I will keep this short because I am tried of writing it out again and again only to lose it.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy has been the dominant force in MtAs, they haven't actually gotten closer to achieving their goals in over at least a hundred years. Not because of the Mages or other Supernaturals but because of the Masses. Yes, the Masses have embraced Technology but that's really all they have. Science-denying Flat-Earthers and Anti-vaxxers not only still exist but are thriving. Hate-mongering nationalists and religious fundamentalists endure and rally against the unified, scientific world they wish to create.<br /> <br /> In the end, the Union is now stuck dealing with the various Supernatural threats and mundane problems like climate change while also having to fight against the stupidity and willful ignorance of the Masses.<br /> <br /> Hell, the introduction of <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> starts with this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A far cry from the more triumphant introduction of it's predecessor, <i>Guide to the Technocracy</i>. And throughout the book we get other Technocrats just frustrated with the Masses over their willful apathy and ignorance. In one section, a veteran field operative describes humanity stupidity as the worst thing that any agent will encounter, as while the supernaturals can cause all manner of headaches, they haven't started world wars or endangered the planet with nuclear Armageddon.<br /> <br /> It's also a bit of a continuation of the collective apathy of the Masses from Rev Ed where no one really won the Ascension War and it ended up largely being a pointless waste because the Masses decided that they didn't care about all that Ascension business and would rather wallow in the mud of apathy and ignorance.<br /> <br /> I will also add that while the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani haven't really held out all that well against the Technocracy, the Disparate Alliance might actually be a real success for them and more importantly, are targeting a much more serious threat to the world, the Nephandi. Who have kind of become a blind spot for the Traditions and Technocracy. Yes, both do fight them but not nearly as much as they do each other. And depending on your Metaplot setup, may have become the unwitting dupes of the Nephandi. So one could argue that while the Traditions and Technocracy have become fixated on their conflict and a goal that is perhaps impossible, even for Mages, the Disparates are focusing their attention to a much real threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arent, the books supposed to have unreliable narrators? Could'nt the explanation given by the agent simply be an opinion and not an objective fact? Because a lot of the reasons given for why the technocracy hasnt won seem to be attributed to a vocal minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T20:59:03-07:00","id":1518408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518346#post1518346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arent, the books supposed to have unreliable narrators? Could'nt the explanation given by the agent simply be an opinion and not an objective fact? Because a lot of the reasons given for why the technocracy hasnt won seem to be attributed to a vocal minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vocal minority? I assume you're not talking globally because last time I checked, Sleepers are a majority of the human race.<br /> <br /> As for locally, it depends on the region because as powerful as Technocracy is, they don't have infinite resources (more so in a post-Avatar Storm world) and so they have to ration what resources go where. If they wanted to, they could throw a ton of resources at the Middle East and crush the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani there. However that would cost them in other regions across the globe as it would mean forcing the resources those places need to the Middle East which will in turn cause more problems. Cause that's the thing, the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani in the Middle East only need to defend the places they hold from the Technocracy. Technocracy has to defend everything they hold across the globe and beyond from many enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T04:33:54-07:00","id":1518423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518408#post1518408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vocal minority? I assume you're not talking globally because last time I checked, Sleepers are a majority of the human race.<br /> <br /> As for locally, it depends on the region because as powerful as Technocracy is, they don't have infinite resources (more so in a post-Avatar Storm world) and so they have to ration what resources go where. If they wanted to, they could throw a ton of resources at the Middle East and crush the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani there. However that would cost them in other regions across the globe as it would mean forcing the resources those places need to the Middle East which will in turn cause more problems. Cause that's the thing, the Ahl-I-Batin and Taftani in the Middle East only need to defend the places they hold from the Technocracy. Technocracy has to defend everything they hold across the globe and beyond from many enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say vocal minority, I was refering to the reasons given for why the technocratic paradigm isnt more widespread &quot;Man is fundamentally irrational. He wants ghosts and vampires and boy wizards with English accents. He wants to believe that genital configurations or melanin production define him as blessed in the eyes of nonexistent gods. He doesn\u2019t fear Apocalypse \u2014 he craves it, so long as he doesn\u2019t have to live personally with the results. He\u2019s more fascinated with wanking off in the mirror than with looking toward the horizon of what he could be if he\u2019d just get his hand off his cock&quot; is being attributed to a vocal minority. Some of the stuff said doesent make sense either and feels like I am reading a post from r/athiest. They are attaking a cariculture instead of a real issue.<br /> <br /> It doesent talk about stuff like how many African Americans dont trust the healthcare system due to attrocities that were done against them in the past. The Antebellum period saw disections, examinations, grave robbing, experimentaions, the &quot;psychiactric diagnoses&quot; of run away slave syndrome, and later the Tuskeegee incident. IDK if the book goes into all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T12:11:18-07:00","id":1518553,"title":"","content":"What's the point of asking a question and then disputing the validity of every single answer you get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T12:28:09-07:00","id":1518559,"title":"","content":"Because they already know what they want the answer to be and people aren\u2019t giving it to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T18:17:59-07:00","id":1518591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518553#post1518553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point of asking a question and then disputing the validity of every single answer you get?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I feel the answer could be challenged, should I not challenge it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-22-2023, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T05:18:05-07:00","id":1518634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518591#post1518591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I feel the answer could be challenged, should I not challenge it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked a question. People gave you responses based on the material in the books and their experience in running the game. You proceeded to disagree with everyone without engaging in discussion but just hammering your thesis. Why ask for discussion if you have already decided on an answer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T10:10:57-07:00","id":1518644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518634#post1518634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You asked a question. People gave you responses based on the material in the books and their experience in running the game. You proceeded to disagree with everyone without engaging in discussion but just hammering your thesis. Why ask for discussion if you have already decided on an answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>What question did I ask exactly? I made a statement, and then tried to defend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-23-2023, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T07:24:25-07:00","id":1518755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518423#post1518423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say vocal minority, I was refering to the reasons given for why the technocratic paradigm isnt more widespread &quot;Man is fundamentally irrational. He wants ghosts and vampires and boy wizards with English accents. He wants to believe that genital configurations or melanin production define him as blessed in the eyes of nonexistent gods. He doesn\u2019t fear Apocalypse \u2014 he craves it, so long as he doesn\u2019t have to live personally with the results. He\u2019s more fascinated with wanking off in the mirror than with looking toward the horizon of what he could be if he\u2019d just get his hand off his cock&quot; is being attributed to a vocal minority. Some of the stuff said doesent make sense either and feels like I am reading a post from r/athiest. They are attaking a cariculture instead of a real issue.<br /> <br /> It doesent talk about stuff like how many African Americans dont trust the healthcare system due to attrocities that were done against them in the past. The Antebellum period saw disections, examinations, grave robbing, experimentaions, the &quot;psychiactric diagnoses&quot; of run away slave syndrome, and later the Tuskeegee incident. IDK if the book goes into all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that it's an IOC introduction from someone that presumably it's on the Technocracy's side, it shouldn't be considered poor if doesn't mention evils that could be easily atributable to the Technocracy or their favored system/ideologies. If it reads like an r/athiest, that's not wrong because it may as well be one.<br /> <br /> BUT they're aknowleging something that has been discussed in the Forums for years on: How it's that the Technocracy is wining when most of the world it's religious or at least superstitious?<br /> <br /> It happens that people does believe in technology (in practice, altrough most often don't understand/care about the theory), but also believe in all those things that the technocracy would rather have the Consensus against.<br /> <br /> Anty-vaxxers may be a vocal minority (not quite as small as I would like, though). But devotees of various religions are not. Of course it sounds better to rally against the former and not the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-25-2023, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T08:24:56-07:00","id":1518758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518755#post1518755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember that it's an IOC introduction from someone that presumably it's on the Technocracy's side, it shouldn't be considered poor if doesn't mention evils that could be easily atributable to the Technocracy or their favored system/ideologies. If it reads like an r/athiest, that's not wrong because it may as well be one.<br /> <br /> BUT they're aknowleging something that has been discussed in the Forums for years on: How it's that the Technocracy is wining when most of the world it's religious or at least superstitious?<br /> <br /> It happens that people does believe in technology (in practice, altrough most often don't understand/care about the theory), but also believe in all those things that the technocracy would rather have the Consensus against.<br /> <br /> Anty-vaxxers may be a vocal minority (not quite as small as I would like, though). But devotees of various religions are not. Of course it sounds better to rally against the former and not the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that makes sense. I actually skimmed through Technocracy Reloaded. Its pretty interesting, I do have some hang ups regarding the lore and metaplot, but it is still pretty informative. Hopefully Lore of the Tradtions is just as good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T16:44:51-07:00","id":1518791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518755#post1518755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BUT they're aknowleging something that has been discussed in the Forums for years on: How it's that the Technocracy is wining when most of the world it's religious or at least superstitious?<br /> <br /> It happens that people does believe in technology (in practice, altrough most often don't understand/care about the theory), but also believe in all those things that the technocracy would rather have the Consensus against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to Technocracy's influence, capabilities, methods, and resources, mundane humans also believe in and attribute meaning to :<br /> the government<br /> psychology and sociology<br /> the international community<br /> business corporations<br /> public government sponsored workers and specialists<br /> urban nature areas and ecology<br /> understandable and enjoyable mass popular entertainment<br /> <br /> ...And there are also other ideas, concepts, notions, philosophies, plans, and schemes.<br /> <br /> Certainly inventions, industry, progress, and technology are important, but there are also areas of interest, influence, and focus held by the five Conventions.<br /> It is the responsibility of individual Enlightened Scientists to choose what to promote, focus on, and to improve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T19:19:07-07:00","id":1522983,"title":"","content":"I'm sure the Order of Hermes questions on the Council's competence, like, why aren't they in control?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T08:26:56-07:00","id":1523033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1522983#post1522983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure the Order of Hermes questions on the Council's competence, like, why aren't they in control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like all other humans, the Heremetics are flawed. And it is in our priorities that flaws become most glaringly obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T07:39:19-07:00","id":1523410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517804-ahl-i-batin-and-taftani-s-success-makes-me-question-the-council-of-nines-competence?p=1518755#post1518755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember that it's an IOC introduction from someone that presumably it's on the Technocracy's side, it shouldn't be considered poor if doesn't mention evils that could be easily atributable to the Technocracy or their favored system/ideologies. If it reads like an r/athiest, that's not wrong because it may as well be one.<br /> <br /> BUT they're aknowleging something that has been discussed in the Forums for years on: How it's that the Technocracy is wining when most of the world it's religious or at least superstitious?<br /> <br /> It happens that people does believe in technology (in practice, altrough most often don't understand/care about the theory), but also believe in all those things that the technocracy would rather have the Consensus against.<br /> <br /> Anty-vaxxers may be a vocal minority (not quite as small as I would like, though). But devotees of various religions are not. Of course it sounds better to rally against the former and not the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the premises of the game are just flat out wrong. Most people believe in ghosts and spirits and angels and devas and djins and kamis and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Skeptical Materialist Atheists are actually a very very small percentage of the population, even on developed countries. Most people who are not devout followers of a religion are NOT the sort of skeptical materialists like myself who believe in Science and nothing but Science. Most people would actually consider themselves &quot;non religious&quot; - which just means they don't go to the church every Sunday, yet they either believe in Jesus or Allah or Buddha, or they devise their own &quot;personal spirituality&quot; upon which they just concoct a ton of esoteric and New Age stuff in their own heads.<br /> <br /> That's VASTLY different from the world proposed in the MtA books.<br /> <br /> I mean yes, nobody doubt that a car or a TV or a computer works... And that should serve as &quot;proof&quot; that the Technocratic paradigm is at full swing and that Consensus is reached, however it makes no sense for Angelic or Demonic beings not to be walking on NY's Central Park at broad day light.<br /> <br /> Besides, the reason to why cars and computers to work irl is NOT because we all collectively agree that they should, but rather we all agree that they function is because we have all experienced them working. The game reverses the causality - mostly because MtA in specific and the entirety o WoD in general is almost as good as Gnosticism/Hermeticism propaganda (heck, Demon the Fallen literally has the figure of the Gnostic Demiurge).<br /> <br /> When we play, we just ignore that blatant disregard of reality thou, and we keep our suspension of disbelief while we disconnect the scenario from what realism would mandate for it, and we have fun with it nonetheless.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T09:23:15-07:00","id":1524390,"title":"","content":"I never saw the Council of Nine as particularly competent, and had no issue seeing the Taftani and Batini get into trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-20T16:05:46-07:00","id":1558956,"title":"","content":"For a long period the <b>Order of Reason </b>and its successor <b>The Technocracy</b> had dynamic goals and viable ideals. There were downsides, but living by the other guy's rules were more brutal. Now the <b>Technocracy</b> is facing its contradictions. The stumbling of the Technos is giving both the long stagnant Traditions and the newly formed Alliance there chances. <br /> <br /> Frankly <b>The Order of the Nine Traditions </b>looks more like a functional team than <b>The Disparate Alliance. </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T17:44:05-07:00","id":1560773,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've finally read the <i>Lost Paths </i>and know a little bit more about the Taftani: Ok, so, I don't really, &quot;Do&quot;, the mage meta-plot, for Mage per se, but I have read a lot of books about Islamic and pre-Islamic Arabia; <i>Arabia and the Arabs</i> by Robert Hoyland is a nice book to read. I see more of a Batin vs Taftani theme as, with Batin's concept of Unity, being united under Islam, and the Taftani's belief in Spirits, and proof of polytheism as more of a conflict, then the technocracy, that can only penetrate into the Arab cities, at best. And, then the oil goes, so does the wealth and technocracy's influence.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I don't believe the Djinn are immune from being bound to a fetish. Mages can do anything ANYTHING. And the Djinn haven't met a wendigo yet (not the tribe, the spirit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}